<title>HUNGARY: Skala plans to sell 60,000 own shrs in H1.</title>
<headline>Skala plans to sell 60,000 own shrs in H1.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian holding company Skala-Coop Rt announced on Monday it planned to sell 60,000 own shares in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>The company did not provide further details on its plans.</p>
<p>However, in late January Skala-Coop said it planned to sell 10,000 own shares in the first quarter of the year.</p>
<p>Last Friday Skala shares closed at 2,300 forints, down 300, on the Budapest Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>Skala is majority owned by Germany's Tengelmann AG.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
